    "faq_CweLwV": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_frrE7e": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Part-Time Contractor — Social Media & Community Manager (Miami)",
            "content": "<h4>About The Conscious Bar</h4><p>The Conscious Bar is redefining chocolate as a nourishing pleasure—built on real ingredients, real education, and real community.</p><p></p><h4>The Role (Contractor)</h4><p>You’ll own the <em>day-to-day execution</em> of our organic social presence and community. You are not the lead strategist, but you are the person who makes the plan come alive: posting consistently, engaging the community in real time, and capturing native content when needed.</p><p></p><h4>Key Responsibilities</h4><p><strong>Publishing + Scheduling</strong></p><ul><li>Manage scheduling and posting across all organic platforms (Instagram, TikTok, etc.).</li><li>Own the publishing calendar and ensure consistency across channels.</li><li>Coordinate with Creative Director/creative team to receive assets and post on time.</li></ul><p><strong>Captions + Platform Execution</strong></p><ul><li>Write/edit platform-specific captions in TCB voice (clean, minimal, witty, educational when needed).</li><li>Handle tagging, hashtags, geo-tags (Miami), and platform-native formatting best practices.</li><li>Maintain organized workflows for assets, drafts, approvals, and versioning.</li></ul><p><strong>Community Management (Comments + DMs)</strong></p><ul><li>Respond to comments across platforms quickly and in brand voice.</li><li>Respond to DMs, triage support needs, and escalate when necessary.</li><li>Track FAQs, objections, and recurring community themes; report insights weekly.</li></ul><p><strong>Stories Posting + Community Building</strong></p><ul><li>Post Stories daily: scheduled assets + timely, “in the moment” content.</li><li>Keep Stories feeling alive using polls, question boxes, quizzes, reposts, UGC, and community prompts.</li><li>Maintain Story hygiene (high frequency, low friction, native feel).</li></ul><p><strong>Native iPhone Content Capture (A Must)</strong></p><ul><li>Shoot native-to-platform iPhone content as needed (Stories/Reels/TikTok style).</li><li>Capture quick BTS, in-store moments, team moments, product moments, and Miami lifestyle moments.</li><li>Maintain strong composition, lighting, framing, and aesthetic consistency with the brand.</li><li>Coordinate with team occasionally to record certain moments/content when prompted.</li></ul><p><strong>Trend + Culture Fluency</strong></p><ul><li>Stay current on organic IG/TikTok trends, platform features, editing styles, and cultural moments.</li><li>Understand internet language, memes, sounds, formats, pop culture, and “what’s hitting right now.”</li><li>Bring trend opportunities to the team (lightweight suggestions + “we should post this today” instincts).</li></ul><p><strong>On-Camera Presence</strong></p><ul><li>Comfortable filming selfie-style clips and appearing on camera when needed (quick community updates, story Q&As, reactions, etc.).</li></ul><h4>Requirements</h4><ul><li><strong>Miami local</strong> (in-person availability as needed).</li><li>Strong experience running organic IG + TikTok (you know them like the back of your hand).</li><li>Excellent on-camera comfort + confident, natural presence.</li><li>Strong iPhone shooting skills + a great eye for aesthetics (framing, lighting, vibe).</li><li>Deep cultural fluency: trends, pop culture, and social media moments.</li><li>Health + wellness nerd energy (ingredients, labels, wellness lifestyle familiarity).</li><li>Loves chocolate (genuinely).</li></ul><h4>Nice-to-Haves</h4><ul><li>Light editing skills (CapCut, Reels/TikTok native edits, subtitles).</li><li>Experience with wellness/CPG brands.</li><li>UGC instincts and creator coordination experience.</li></ul><h4>Time Commitment</h4><ul><li>Part-time contractor (typical range: ~10–20 hrs/week depending on content volume).</li><li>Some weekend responsiveness may be required for community.</li></ul><h4>Success Looks Like</h4><ul><li>We post consistently without gaps.</li><li>Comments/DMs feel fast, warm, at times witty and “real.”</li><li>Stories feel like a community hub (not just announcements)<br/></li><li>IG Lives + Live Shopping moments now and then</li><li>Native iPhone content adds freshness and cultural relevance.</li></ul><h4>Contractor Note</h4><p>This is a <strong>1099 contractor</strong> position.</p>",
            "button_label": "Apply Now",
            "button_link": "https://form.typeform.com/to/cppC6K3O"
          }
        },
        "item_APi8Hg": {
          "type": "item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "title": "Growth Marketing Manager",
            "content": "<p><strong>Job Title:</strong> Graphics Designer<strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p><strong>Job Type:</strong> Part-time, Monthly Contract</p><p><strong>Experience Level:</strong> Intermediate (1–2 years)</p><p><strong>Salary:</strong> Negotiable</p><p><strong>About Batin Studio:</strong><br/>Batin Studio is a dynamic digital product design and development agency specializing in creating bespoke e‑commerce solutions and brand experiences. We design and build products that help our clients stand out in the crowded online marketplace.</p><p><strong>Role Overview:</strong><br/>We are looking for an experienced Graphics Designer to join our team on a part-time, contract basis. You’ll be responsible for creating compelling visual assets across social media, marketing campaigns, and other brand touchpoints. </p><p><br/></p><p><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><p></p><ul><li>Design high-quality static posts, carousels, story packs, and promotional graphics for social media channels.</li><li>Create product cut‑outs, hero images, and other visual assets that align with brand guidelines.</li><li>Work closely with our design lead to translate concepts into polished visuals.</li><li>Organize design files for easy reuse and iteration.</li><li>Ensure all designs adhere to brand aesthetics, typography, and color palettes.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><p></p><ul><li>1–2 years of professional graphic design experience.</li><li>Proficiency with Figma and at least one of Canva, Photoshop, or Illustrator.</li><li>Strong portfolio demonstrating social media design and visual storytelling.</li><li>Excellent attention to detail, layout, and composition.</li><li>Ability to manage multiple projects and deliver on time.</li><li>Clear written and verbal communication skills.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Contract & Growth:</strong></p><p></p><ul><li>This role is structured as a monthly contract (~15–20 hours/week).</li><li>After two months, we’ll review performance with the option of transitioning to a full-time position.</li><li>Salary is negotiable based on experience and demonstrated skill.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>How to Apply: </strong>Interested candidates are invited to submit their resume and portfolio through the following Google Form: https://forms.gle/uibUHdQJKPaHPVA99</p><p><strong>Application Deadline:</strong> 20th September, 2025</p><p>Batin Studio is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.</p>",
